The mysterious force comes as soon as you have got the Amulet, not
earlier.

What I do is to levelport from the Valley to some level number that
exceeds the maximum, thereby knowing that I've reached the VS level
where I have to step on quite every square to locate the entrance.
At that deep levels I typically meet some purple liches, hit them
until they flee to the upstairs; that way I can locate the stairs
while blindfolded without exploring the level or writing and using
scrolls (or spells) of magic mapping, rinse repeat. That's a very
fast way to cross Gehennom! At some choosen point (e.g. when you're
annoyed by the L's, or when you've explored enough of Gehennom to
cover the rest of of the stairs detection with your scrolls, or if
a couple liches accumulated) you can genocide them and may get a
very useful athame if you're lucky.
Once you've reached the lowest level where Vlad can be, use one of
your scarce scrolls of magic mapping (or write one), continue while
you're in Vlad's possible level interval and until you found a level
with two stairs. Handle Vlad, then levelport to level 1 to prepare
the final steps (get the Book, get the Amulet, climb up).
The missing, yet unexplored levels, the ones between Vlad and the
Valley, are quickly explored with the Amulets clairvoyance property
that you have at that time, or mapped with more scrolls (or spells),
as desired.
At least Juiblex' and Asmodeus' levels are always, and Baalzebub's
level mostly, in the unexplored level range; so you don't need many
scrolls to map those levels, because the general layout is well known.
(And Juiblex will also serve you as a transporter across the swamp if
handled with care, just BTW.)

All in all a very quick traversal of Gehennom.

